---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import HeaderBand from "../components/HeaderBand.astro";
import PageTitle from "../components/PageTitle.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About | Altair R."
  description="About Altair R., a software engineer who works across backend, infra, reliability, and the awkward edges between systems."
>
  <HeaderBand active="about" />

  <main class="content-main">
    <header class="page-header">
      <PageTitle title="About" icon="compass" />
    </header>

    <section class="about-body">
      <p>Fourteen years writing software, most of it spent on the parts of a system nobody wanted to claim: the migration, the retry logic, the pager. I've been backend, infra, and once for a bad quarter, half of a frontend team - not because I'm hard to place, but because whatever was on fire needed someone who had already fixed something like it. I grew up moving between four cities and never fully lost the habit; I still do not buy furniture I would mind leaving behind. I run, badly, in the mornings before the pager has a chance to weigh in on my day, and I read more nonfiction than I finish. Currently a staff engineer, still on the pager, still not sure that is a title and not a description of a personality flaw.</p>
      <figure class="portrait">
        <img src="/assets/images/portrait.jpg" alt="Altair R.">
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section class="about-contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
      <h2 id="contact-title">Contact</h2>
      <p><code>altairrostam [at] gmail [dot] com</code></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
